# The shipping build talks to the hosted org — the account's agents, projects,
# knowledge and history live there, not on this machine. What stays local is the
# harness: the Hermes gateway the shell starts, which runs the work.
#
# This is only a DEFAULT. api.ts resolves the host on every call and a stored
# value wins, so the same artifact can be pointed at a self-hosted server or a
# local one from the sign-in screen. Loaded by `vite build --mode shipping`
# (npm run build:shipping); plain `npm run build` keeps the dev default.
VITE_AULAR_API=https://api.aular.app
